md('## 11. Regime Sensitivity\n\nBreaks at 1984 and 2000 are **descriptive**, not optimized to select the most favorable regime. The evaluation set omits early decades due to minimum training. Leave-one-decade-out below excludes the named decade from OOS *scoring* while preserving the original historical training process; it is not a refit with that decade removed from training.')
code("regime=pd.read_csv('results/regime_sensitivity.csv');display(regime.round(4))")
code("leave=pd.read_csv('results/leave_one_decade_out.csv');display(leave.round(4))")
md('## 12. Bias Audit & Verdict\n\n**Look-ahead:** target purging and feature lags checked, but release-vintage leakage remains UNKNOWN. **Selection:** aggregate PCE was selected after reviewing existing industries; results are exploratory. **Survivorship:** not applicable to the aggregate series, but no historical firm universe exists. **Multiple testing:** several robustness choices reported without familywise adjustment; treat favorable findings cautiously. **Costs/capacity:** no tradable strategy was specified, so costs cannot be assessed. **Verdict:** use the observed OOS and uncertainty results, not the economic story, to determine whether the hypothesis survives; no investable equity alpha is claimed.')
code("print('Control RMSE',round(metrics['control_rmse'],4),'Augmented RMSE',round(metrics['augmented_rmse'],4),'gain',round(metrics['gain_log_pp'],4));print('Bootstrap 95% CI',metrics['bootstrap_ci95']);print('NOT PIT:',not metrics['pit_verified'],'NO firm fundamentals:',not metrics['company_fundamentals_tested'],'NO equity returns:',not metrics['security_total_returns_tested'])")
md('## 13. Reproduction\n\nFrom a clean checkout, install `requirements.txt`, run `python run_analysis.py`, then `python -m pytest -q tests`, and execute the notebook with `jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute research.ipynb --output executed.ipynb`. The committed notebook includes actual computed outputs. Numeric results are deterministic under the stated RNG seeds, library environment and frozen CSV; exact image bytes can vary with matplotlib/font versions.')
